  21:     Rule
  22:     - If the rectangles are side-by-side, color the left half of the inter-object gap across every row with the left object's color, and the right half with the right object's color.
  23:     - If one rectangle is above the other, color the upper half of the gap across every column with the upper object's color, and the lower half with the lower object's color.
  24:     - When the gap length is odd, leave the center row/column as background.
  25: 
  26:     Key insight
  27:     - The marker objects are endpoints of an axial corridor; their own size identifies the facing edge, while the filled corridor spans the whole grid perpendicular to that axis.
  28:     """
